###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table S1 is headed 'absolute force and energy errors'; the methods section calls them mean absolute errors, so they are encoded as MAE. Energy errors are in eV per atom (no vocabulary unit; in the label). The foundation-model energy 'errors' (hundreds of eV per atom) are reference-energy offsets and are not encoded; the foundation-model force errors are in the result comments because the foundation models are not pinned to a release (MACE-MP-0, SevenNet-0 and MatterSim each have several registry or candidate checkpoints).
# - Fine-tuning from a foundation model is a string-valued setting; schema 0.1.2 has no base-model relation. SevenNet runs are placed under the registry method NequIP and MatterSim runs under M3GNet, following the registry rows of SevenNet-0 and MatterSim-v1; GRACE-1L is the one-layer GRACE.
# - The exchange-correlation functional per system (BLYP or PBE) and the exact train/validation/test split per run (70-90% training) are not given in the text read. Table S2 has no MoS2 row. Derived properties (RDFs, diffusion coefficients, autocorrelation functions) and MD timings (Table S3) are not encoded.
# - Read from the arXiv v1 preprint.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

